J half-widths are maximum available per-trial quantization, edge enclosures (counter increments or Pmax times the two inward edge-to-poll distances), clock and averaging bounds, conditional on piecewise-linear interior power and a recorded maximum for power traces. They are not confidence intervals on the mean or sensor-accuracy bounds. An absent half-width means an unknown/unbounded term, including duty-cycle gaps; missing trials are counted. Seeds have separate Wilson rows; repeated items are never pooled as independent.
For powermetrics, D-078's 1 J attribution minimum applies once to each trial's summed total across the selected disjoint rails, after adding their modeled bounds; it is not added once per rail.

